G1839.b:
† ⟪ἐξ-ίστημι⟫ (also in Hellenistic -ιστάνω, ⟦Acts 8:9|Ac 8:9⟧),
[in LXX for⁨חרד⁩, etc. (29 words in all) ;],
⟪1.⟫ causal in pres., impf., fut., 1 aor., ⟪to put out of its place⟫; metaph., ἐ. τινά φρενῶν (Eur.), ⟪to drive one out of his senses, hence⟫, absol., ⟪to confound, amaze⟫: c. acc pers., ⟦Luke 24:22|Lk 24:22⟧, ⟦Acts 8:9|Ac 8:9⟧, ⟦Acts 8:11|11⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Intr. in pass. and mid., also in 2 aor., pf., plpf. act., seq. ἐκ or c. gen., ⟪to stand aside from, retire from⟫; esp. τ. φρενῶν,⟪to lose one's senses⟫ (Eur.), hence, absol.;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to be beside oneself, be mad⟫: ⟦Mark 3:21|Mk 3:21⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:13|II Co 5:13⟧ (opp. to σωφρονεῖν);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to be amazed, confounded⟫: ⟦Matthew 12:23|Mt 12:23⟧, ⟦Mark 2:12|Mk 2:12⟧ ⟦Mark 5:42|5:42⟧ ⟦Mark 6:51|6:51⟧, ⟦Luke 2:47|Lk 2:47⟧ ⟦Luke 8:56|8:56⟧, ⟦Acts 2:7|Ac 2:7⟧, ⟦Acts 2:12|12⟧ ⟦Acts 8:13|8:13⟧ ⟦Acts 9:21|9:21⟧ ⟦Acts 10:45|10:45⟧ ⟦Acts 12:16|12:16⟧ (Cremer, 309).†

G1854.b:
⟪ἔξω⟫ adv.
(< ἐξ), [in LXX for ⁨חוּץ⁩ ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪outside, without⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ adverbially: ⟦Matthew 12:46|Mt 12:46⟧, ⟦Mark 3:31|Mk 3:31⟧ ⟦Mark 11:4|11:4⟧, ⟦Luke 8:20|Lk 8:20⟧, ⟦John 18:16|Jo 18:16⟧, al.; c. art., ὁ ἔ., ⟪he who is without⟫; metaph., in pl., οἱ ἔ., of those outside the Church, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:12|I Co 5:12⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:13|13⟧, ⟦Colossians 4:5|Col 4:5⟧ (Lft., in l), ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:12|I Th 4:12⟧; ὁ ἔ. ἄνθρωπος, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:16|II Co 4:16⟧; αἱ ἔ. πόλεις, ⟦Acts 26:11|Ac 26:11⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ as prep. c. gen.: ⟦Luke 13:33|Lk 13:33⟧, ⟦Acts 21:5|Ac 21:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:11|He 13:11⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:12|12⟧
⟪2.⟫ After verbs of motion;
⟪(a)⟫ adverbially, ⟪forth, out⟫: ⟦Matthew 5:13|Mt 5:13⟧ ⟦Mark 14:68|Mk 14:68⟧, ⟦Luke 22:62|Lk 22:62⟧, ⟦John 6:37|Jo 6:37⟧ ⟦John 19:4|19:4⟧, ⟦John 19:13|13⟧, ⟦Acts 9:40|Ac 9:40⟧, al.;
⟪(b)⟫ as prep. c. gen., ⟪out of⟫: ⟦Matthew 21:17|Mt 21:17⟧, ⟦Mark 11:19|Mk 11:19⟧ ⟦Mark 12:8|12:8⟧, ⟦Luke 4:29|Lk 4:29⟧, ⟦Acts 7:58|Ac 7:58⟧, ⟦Hebrews 13:13|He 13:13⟧, al

G1861.b:
⟪ἐπ-αγγέλλω⟫
[in LXX: ⟦Ezra 4:8|Es 4:8⟧ (⁨אָמַר⁩), ⟦Proverbs 13:12|Pr 13:12⟧, Wi 2:13, al. ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to announce, proclaim⟫.
⟪2.⟫
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to promise⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to profess⟫. Mid., also freq. in both these senses;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪to promise⟫: c. dat. pers., ⟦Hebrews 6:13|He 6:13⟧; c. acc rei, ⟦Romans 4:21|Ro 4:21⟧, ⟦Titus 1:2|Tit 1:2⟧; c. dat pers. et acc rei, ⟦James 1:12|Ja 1:12⟧ ⟦James 2:5|2:5⟧, ⟦2 Peter 2:19|II Pe 2:19⟧; ἐπαγγελίαν, ⟦1 John 2:25|I Jo 2:25⟧; c. inf., ⟦Mark 14:11|Mk 14:11⟧, ⟦Acts 7:5|Ac 7:5⟧; seq. λέγων, ⟦Hebrews 12:26|He 12:26⟧; ptcp., ⟦Hebrews 10:23|He 10:23⟧ ⟦Hebrews 11:11|11:11⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ ⟪to profess⟫: θεοσέβειαν, ⟦1 Timothy 2:10|I Ti 2:10⟧; γνῶσιν, ⟦1 Timothy 6:21|I Ti 6:21⟧. Pass., ⟦Galatians 3:19|Ga 3:19⟧ (cf. προ-επαγγέλλω; and v. Cremer, 26).†

G1864.b:
⟪ἐπ-αγωνίζομαι⟫ depon.;
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to contend with⟫ (Plut.).
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to contend for⟫ (C.I., 2335, 19): c. dat. rei, ⟦Jude 1:3|Ju 3⟧.†

G1883.b:
⟪ἐπ-άνω⟫ adv.,
[in LXX for ⁨מַעֲלָה⁩, ⁨עַל⁩, ⁨מֵעָל⁩, etc. ;] ⟪above⟫;
⟪1.⟫ adverbially;
⟪(a)⟫ of place: ⟦Luke 11:44|Lk 11:44⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of number, ⟪more than⟫: ⟦Mark 14:5|Mk 14:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:6|I Co 15:6⟧.
⟪2.⟫ As prep. c. gen.;
⟪(a)⟫ of place: ⟦Matthew 2:9|Mt 2:9⟧ ⟦Matthew 5:14|5:14⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:7|21:7⟧ ⟦Matthew 23:18|23:18⟧, ⟦Matthew 23:20|20⟧, ⟦Matthew 23:22|22⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:37|27:37⟧ ⟦Matthew 28:2|28:2⟧, ⟦Luke 4:39|Lk 4:39⟧ ⟦Luke 10:19|10:19⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:8|Re 6:8⟧ ⟦Revelation 20:3|20:3⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of pre-eminence: ⟦Luke 19:17|Lk 19:17⟧, ⟦Luke 19:19|19⟧, ⟦John 3:31|Jo 3:31⟧.†

G1893.b:
⟪ἐπεί⟫ conj. (ἐπί, εἰ), ⟪when, since⟫;
⟪1.⟫ of time, ⟪when, after⟫: ⟦Luke 7:1|Lk 7:1⟧ (Rec., WH, mg.).
⟪2.⟫ Of cause, ⟪since, because⟫: ⟦Matthew 18:32|Mt 18:32⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:46|21:46⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:6|27:6⟧, ⟦Mark 15:42|Mk 15:42⟧, ⟦Luke 1:34|Lk 1:34⟧, ⟦John 13:29|Jo 13:29⟧ ⟦John 19:31|19:31⟧, ⟦Acts 13:46|Ac 13:46⟧ (Rec., WH, mg.), ⟦1 Corinthians 14:12|I Co 14:12⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:18|II Co 11:18⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 13:3|13:3⟧, ⟦Hebrews 5:2|He 5:2⟧, ⟦Hebrews 5:11|11⟧ ⟦Hebrews 6:13|6:13⟧ ⟦Hebrews 9:17|9:17⟧ ⟦Hebrews 11:11|11:11⟧; ἐ. οὖν, ⟦Hebrews 2:14|He 2:14⟧ ⟦Hebrews 4:6|4:6⟧. With ellipsis, ⟪otherwise, else⟫: ⟦Romans 11:6|Ro 11:6⟧, ⟦Romans 11:22|22⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:26|He 9:26⟧; ἐ. ἄρα, ⟦1 Corinthians 5:10|I Co 5:10⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 7:14|7:14⟧; introducing a question, ⟦Romans 3:6|Ro 3:6⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:16|I Co 14:16⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 15:29|15:29⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:2|He 10:2⟧ (cf. IV Mac 1:33 2:7 2:10 4:24, 26).†

G1894.b:
⟪ἐπει-δή⟫ conj.;
⟪1.⟫ of time, ⟪when now, after that⟫: ⟦Luke 7:1|Lk 7:1⟧ (WH, txt.).
⟪2.⟫ Of cause, ⟪seeing that, forasmuch as⟫: ⟦Luke 11:6|Lk 11:6⟧, ⟦Acts 13:46|Ac 13:46⟧ (WH, txt., RV) ⟦Acts 14:12|Ac 14:12⟧ ⟦Acts 15:24|15:24⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:21|I Co 1:21⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:22|22⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 14:16|14:16⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 15:21|15:21⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:26|Phl 2:26⟧.†
